-- a date picker holds a day --
  every platform cortado builds for has one: true
  any instant in a day names that day: true
  and what comes back is always a midnight: true
  a second before the epoch is the day before it: true
  10,000 consecutive days each read back the day written: true
  a day the user picks raises value_changed: true
  and the event carries the day, not the instant: true
  a day the program writes raises nothing: true
-- a colour well holds four bytes --
  every platform cortado builds for has one: true
  all 256 levels of every channel come back unchanged: true
  red is red and not alpha: rgba(255,0,0,255)
  and packs into the high byte: true
  a partly transparent colour keeps its alpha: rgba(0,128,255,64)
  a number above 0xFFFFFFFF is refused: true
  and a negative one: true
  a colour the user picks raises value_changed: true
  and the event carries the packed colour: true
  a colour the program writes raises nothing: true
-- and no other control carries either --
  every kind this platform builds was asked: true
  only a date picker takes a day: true
  only a colour well takes a colour: true
drove=true
